{
  "id": "kinesthetic-feedback",
  "term": "kinesthetic feedback",
  "definition": "Kinesthetic feedback is movement-related sensory input used to reflect the body’s sensorimotor loop and guide actions or imagined actions. In this context, it refers to artificial somatosensory cues, such as vibrotactile input, that provide a more intuitive sense of movement than visual information alone.",
